    "field": "Aerosol-climate interactions",
    "problem": "Existing climate models struggle to quantify the climate impact of Asian aerosols, as global models inadequately resolve cloud-scale processes while regional models fail to capture feedback on the large-scale atmospheric circulation.",
    "method": "The paper proposes a hierarchical modelling approach that incorporates aerosol-induced diabatic heating anomalies, calculated from a regional cloud-resolving model, into a global climate model to quantify the climatic impact of Asian pollution on mid-latitude cyclones and global circulation.",
    "task": "The task is to investigate and quantify the climatic impact of Asian pollution on mid-latitude cyclones by using a novel hierarchical modeling approach combined with observational analysis.",
